          "id": 58,
          "start": 178.07999999999998,
          "end": 180.48,
          "en": "in the same instance in the entire application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 180.48,
          "end": 182.91,
          "en": "because we're using the service in two different components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 182.91,
          "end": 185.01,
          "en": "and yet we're using the same object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.01,
          "end": 187.83,
          "en": "Otherwise last log would be undefined here, as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 187.83,
          "end": 189.54,
          "en": "It isn't, and therefore we have proof",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 189.54,
          "end": 191.343,
          "en": "that it's the same object as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 193.38,
          "end": 196.29,
          "en": "Let's change this by not using @Injectable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 196.29,
          "end": 198.18,
          "en": "we've provided in root, here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 198.18,
          "end": 201.45,
          "en": "But, let's instead provide the service in the app module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 201.45,
          "end": 204.09,
          "en": "There we can add providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 204.09,
          "end": 206.313,
          "en": "and we provide the logging service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 207.24,
          "end": 210.78,
          "en": "Let me switch back to authenticate and reload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 210.78,
          "end": 212.13,
          "en": "Same output as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 212.13,
          "end": 213.36,
          "en": "Let's go to Shopping List.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 213.36,
          "end": 214.71,
          "en": "Same output as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 214.71,
          "end": 218.37,
          "en": "Because providing in the app module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 218.37,
          "end": 221.82,
          "en": "has the same effect as using @Injectable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 221.82,
          "end": 224.04,
          "en": "Let's get rid of that, as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 224.04,
          "end": 228.12,
          "en": "Let's now use an eagerly loaded module, the core module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 228.12,
          "end": 230.01,
          "en": "That is eagerly loaded because we import it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 230.01,
          "end": 231.273,
          "en": "here into the app module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 232.11,
          "end": 235.89,
          "en": "There, well, I already do provide services here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 235.89,
          "end": 238.14,
          "en": "so I kind of think that proves the point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 238.14,
          "end": 241.68,
          "en": "but let's now add the logging service here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 241.68,
          "end": 243.3,
          "en": "add the import, as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 243.3,
          "end": 244.8,
          "en": "Save that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 244.8,
          "end": 246.69,
          "en": "Go to authenticate and reload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 246.69,
          "end": 248.16,
          "en": "Same output as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 248.16,
          "end": 250.563,
          "en": "Go to Shopping List, same output as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 251.46,
          "end": 253.65,
          "en": "Now let's change that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 253.65,
          "end": 256.15,
          "en": "Let's remove logging service from the core module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 257.1,
          "end": 258.1,
          "en": "and let's instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 259.32,
          "end": 262.41,
          "en": "provide it here in the app module as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 262.41,
          "end": 264.3,
          "en": "but let's now also provided it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 264.3,
          "end": 266.13,
          "en": "in the shopping list module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 266.13,
          "end": 267.87,
          "en": "There, I'll add providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 267.87,
          "end": 270.45,
          "en": "and I'll provide the logging service, as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 270.45,
          "end": 273.15,
          "en": "So now I'm providing it in a lazy loaded module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 273.15,
          "end": 274.74,
          "en": "the shopping list module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 274.74,
          "end": 277.593,
          "en": "and in an eagerly loaded module, my app module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 278.90999999999997,
          "end": 281.01,
          "en": "Let's go to authenticate and reload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 281.01,
          "end": 282.51,
          "en": "Same output as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 282.51,
          "end": 284.04,
          "en": "Let's go to Shopping List.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 284.04,
          "end": 286.40999999999997,
          "en": "Oh, now the output is different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 286.40999999999997,
          "end": 288.96,
          "en": "Because we're now using two different objects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 288.96,
          "end": 293.34000000000003,
          "en": "two different instances of that same service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 293.34000000000003,
          "end": 296.67,
          "en": "We're using a separate instance in our application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 296.67,
          "end": 300.51,
          "en": "in general, for the service provided in app module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 300.51,
          "end": 303.75,
          "en": "But since the shopping list module brings its own instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 303.75,
          "end": 306.78,
          "en": "by providing the logging service, again, here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 306.78,
          "end": 309.24,
          "en": "the shopping list module and all the components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 309.24,
          "end": 312.27,
          "en": "in there use a separate instance of the logging service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 312.27,
          "end": 315,
          "en": "They don't use the application wide available instance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 315,
          "end": 318.63,
          "en": "They use their own instance created by that child injector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 318.63,
          "end": 321.33,
          "en": "Now if you need that behavior, definitely use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 321.33,
          "end": 323.37,
          "en": "Nothing wrong with it. This is not a bug.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 323.37,
          "end": 325.32,
          "en": "This is an intended feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 325.32,
          "end": 326.46,
          "en": "But in general,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 326.46,
          "end": 329.91,
          "en": "you should think twice before you provide a service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 329.91,
          "end": 332.73,
          "en": "in any other module than the app module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 332.73,
          "end": 335.04,
          "en": "'Cause often it's not the wanted behavior,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 335.04,
          "end": 337.17,
          "en": "and you then suddenly have strange bugs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 337.17,
          "end": 340.11,
          "en": "when you're using different instances in your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 340.11,
          "end": 343.53,
          "en": "So if you need that behavior, use it, but generally be aware",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 343.53,
          "end": 346.47,
          "en": "that there are differences in the instances you get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 346.47,
          "end": 349.98,
          "en": "when you provide services in lazy loaded modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 349.98,
          "end": 352.83,
          "en": "This also includes modules that you import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 352.83,
          "end": 354.633,
          "en": "into lazy loaded modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 355.56,
          "end": 357.53,
          "en": "For example, if I comment this out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 357.53,
          "end": 359.1,
          "en": "in the shopping list module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 359.1,
          "end": 361.26,
          "en": "and I comment this out in the app module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 361.26,
          "end": 364.68,
          "en": "let's provide the service in the shared module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 364.68,
          "end": 367.89,
          "en": "The shared module here, in the shared folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 367.89,
          "end": 369.66,
          "en": "The shared module, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 369.66,
          "end": 372.45,
          "en": "is always able to add providers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 372.45,
          "end": 375.18,
          "en": "and let's provide the logging service here now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 375.18,
          "end": 378.84,
          "en": "Now the shared module is imported by the app module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 378.84,
          "end": 382.44,
          "en": "and there therefore, it is an eagerly loaded module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 382.44,
          "end": 386.28,
          "en": "but it's also imported into the shopping list module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 386.28,
          "end": 390.15,
          "en": "Now there, the shared module to the shopping list module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 390.15,
          "end": 391.8,
          "en": "is also eagerly loaded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 391.8,
          "end": 394.71,
          "en": "but the shopping list module itself is lazy loaded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 394.71,
          "end": 397.86,
          "en": "turning this here, in this place, the shared module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 397.86,
          "end": 400.8,
          "en": "in this place, also into a lazy loaded module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 400.8,
          "end": 402.93,
          "en": "So here the shared module is both,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 402.93,
          "end": 405.69,
          "en": "it's lazy loaded in the shopping list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 405.69,
          "end": 407.64,
          "en": "or through shopping list module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 407.64,
          "end": 410.578,
          "en": "and it's eagerly loaded into the app module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 410.578,
          "end": 415.35,
          "en": "And the effect is that if we reload here, that works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 415.35,
          "end": 417.81,
          "en": "and we see the output here on the app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 417.81,
          "end": 421.77,
          "en": "but we have the same issue in quotation mark as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 421.77,
          "end": 425.7,
          "en": "because the shopping list module still uses its own instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 425.7,
          "end": 428.73,
          "en": "because it imports the shared module into it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 428.73,
          "end": 433.73,
          "en": "And that is the most problematic bug you often end up with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 433.98,
          "end": 437.22,
          "en": "when providing services in our modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 437.22,
          "end": 439.71,
          "en": "You might be providing a service in something like a",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 439.71,
          "end": 441.72,
          "en": "shared module where you think, Yeah,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 441.72,
          "end": 444.459,
          "en": "I'm going to put all my shared services into this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 444.459,
          "end": 446.88,
          "en": "but you might still have shared services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 446.88,
          "end": 448.32,
          "en": "that should use the same instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 448.32,
          "end": 449.994,
          "en": "across your entire application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 449.994,
          "end": 452.85,
          "en": "Well, as soon as you're importing your shared module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 452.85,
          "end": 454.83,
          "en": "into a lazy loaded module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 454.83,
          "end": 457.47,
          "en": "the services provided in the shared module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 457.47,
          "end": 460.77,
          "en": "will be recreated for the lazy loaded module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 460.77,
          "end": 462.33,
          "en": "And all of a sudden you might have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 462.33,
          "end": 464.31,
          "en": "a behavior you don't want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 464.31,
          "end": 466.29,
          "en": "So whilst providing a service directly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 466.29,
          "end": 467.55,
          "en": "in the lazy loaded module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 467.55,
          "end": 469.83,
          "en": "might be something you control deliberately,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 469.83,
          "end": 472.47,
          "en": "providing it in a shared module is a common gotcha,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 472.47,
          "end": 474.6,
          "en": "where you think you use the same service instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 474.6,
          "end": 476.463,
          "en": "in the entire app when you don't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 477.33,
          "end": 480.03,
          "en": "I know this can be difficult to wrap your head around,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 480.03,
          "end": 483.36,
          "en": "but this is a crucial thing and a common source of bugs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 483.36,
          "end": 485.4,
          "en": "and therefore, the rule of thumb is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 485.4,
          "end": 487.83,
          "en": "that you provide services through @Injectable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 487.83,
          "end": 489.33,
          "en": "or in the app module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 489.33,
          "end": 492.15,
          "en": "If you do it differently, you should have a strong reason",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 492.15,
          "end": 495.9,
          "en": "and you should either be able to rule out that this module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 178,
          "start": 495.9,
          "end": 498.75,
          "en": "you're adding the service in is loaded lazily",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 179,
          "start": 498.75,
          "end": 501.753,
          "en": "or you deliberately want multiple instances.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
